{
  "answer_pre": "Both Doc 2 (fog: Expressing Motion and Emotion through Function Composition of AI-Generated Code) and Doc 3 (Scalable and Culturally Specific Stereotype Dataset Construction via Human-LLM Collaboration) highlight that LLM-generated outputs have limited generalization across contexts—Doc 2 notes the difficulty of expanding to expressive areas beyond motion (e.g., a political campaign) and the challenge of capturing the 'expanse of creative ideas' with natural language prompts, while Doc 3 emphasizes that LLMs struggle to generalize to non-English, low-resource contexts and that cultural specificity is not inherently provided by the models.",
